    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n<p><em>People are glass if you know where to look.</em></p><p>As an <strong>action</strong>, you focus on a creature you can see within <strong>6 squares</strong> and let your own faces flicker in response.</p><ul><li>Make an <strong>Insight (Soul)</strong> check contested by the target’s <strong>Stealth (Intrigue)</strong> (or Presence check, GM’s call).</li><li>On a success, you learn one <strong>useful tag</strong> about the target, chosen by the GM: a primary <strong>fear</strong>, <strong>loyalty</strong>, or <strong>desire</strong> relevant to the current situation.</li><li>On a failure, you get a blurred or partial read; the GM may give you a softer or less precise tag, or hint that the target is unusually opaque.</li></ul><p>This doesn’t expose secrets outright, but it tells you which emotional door is unlocked.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
